#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4640f978-9caa-5960-bec4-f153a1b4cc5d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d86c6bd2-e528-55ed-bbfc-9f5ecbec024e" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5924" :question/problem "Graph the function $y = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1$." :question/worked-solution "To plot\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/2c9172fb7cbb0bd0e0cc81101d0b9923.png)\n\n- Translate it by one unit to the right to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x-1}$.![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/4be35d35282b67338f8ea012d44351e3.png)\nNotice that the vertical asymptote is now $x=1$.\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/ad086b825d99afce3979b91cf20c12ff.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit down to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1$.![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/9e3da682b291a0c948558aca2c22a84a.png)\nNotice that the horizontal asymptote is now $y=-1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "308f3685-0a90-56f3-9653-a83cec4286d2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Some Unknowns Given the Graph of a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ac8b39e3-a9d0-56fd-8c0b-4d748bedf7d4" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5926" :question/problem "The diagram above shows the graph of $y = \\dfrac{a}{x-b}+k$. What is the value of $a+b+k$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/daf6141f9c6d989c76e8b22ea3252d2b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1$, while the vertical asymptote is $x=2$. This means that $k=-1$ and $b=2$, and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}+(-1) = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}-1\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(3,2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{a}{x - 2} - 1 \\\\\n2 &= \\frac{a}{3 - 2} - 1 \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{a}{1} \\\\\na &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b+k = 3+2+(-1) = 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a76e0252-0574-520e-bb5f-43c8faf6a564" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-8658" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x}$." :question/worked-solution "To plot\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{7}{2x}\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/b2b14b94f9894644e75d05697676e241.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\dfrac{7}{2x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/8d7bd88746d1a68547de320e1b6da585.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068580 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e11164-1929-594d-9f9e-460f6469421d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Negative Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a18ff1e7-7f87-5cdd-9a25-91a2e9c1dd5b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-8761" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x}$." :question/worked-solution "To plot\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{1}{5x}\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/044462ee9774b4d1544ef09419972fbd.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac 1 5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{5x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/4b1400c297a6cb4df009ab9ff47ca565.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c47df00-30fe-5707-8d45-5a711f35c4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065939} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c237d4-1aa4-5170-9b04-c52c33f3cd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065940} {:answer/id #uuid "2bad5fb2-1d23-5f74-819e-80bcfee82ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065941} {:answer/id #uuid "443af267-2e0a-5920-8e36-15149b2a1901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065942} {:answer/id #uuid "49596830-be76-5bd3-8461-4c1b4f4de37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443af267-2e0a-5920-8e36-15149b2a1901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/455/Source/Images/q-16506-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065942} :answer-field/id #uuid "73ec280b-ba3b-56b9-bc0c-bf8f37ee1481" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065938}] :question/id #uuid "52bb8cc2-c5a6-51d3-bc88-b